The iPhone Duo's two-app multitasking feature works side by side in landscape, but rotating the inner display to portrait usually drops you back to a single app. However, there is a workaround to keep a video playing above an open app in portrait, and it involves Picture in Picture.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/iphone-duo-pip-video-trick.jpeg" alt="" width="1920" height="1080" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1073368" /><br/>
Both the inner and outer displays on the iPhone Duo share the same 1:1.4 aspect ratio, and each half of the inner display works out to roughly the same size and shape as the outer screen. That even split gives each app a canvas it already has to support, with the divider sitting neatly on the fold. The only apparent exception to this is when watching a TV show or movie above another app in portrait mode – but there's a trick to getting it working.<br/>
<br/>
With your iPhone Duo unfolded in portrait orientation, follow these steps:<br/>
<ol> <li>Start playing a video in an app that supports Picture in Picture, such as Apple TV or Apple Podcasts.</li> <br/>
<li>Tap the Picture in Picture icon to shrink the video into a floating window.<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/iphone-duo-video-portrait-trick2.jpeg" alt="pip" width="1920" height="1080" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1073372" /><br/>
<li>Swipe up to return to the Home Screen, then open the app you want to use (note: it can't be another video app).</li> <br/>
<li>Tap the icon that appears in the PiP window to stack the video above the open app.<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/iphone-duo-video-portrait-trick1.jpeg" alt="pip" width="1920" height="1080" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1073373" /></ol>It's a bit of a fiddle, but it works for most apps that support PiP. Whether Apple makes it a little easier to do in a future update remains to be seen.<div class="linkback">Related Roundup: <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a></div><div class="linkback">Buyer's Guide: <a href="https://buyersguide.macrumors.com/#iPhone-Duo">iPhone Duo (Buy Now)</a></div><div class="linkback">Related Forum: <a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/forums/iphone.99">iPhone</a></div><br/>This article, &quot;<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/how-to/iphone-duo-watch-video-above-app-portrait-mode/">iPhone Duo: Watch Video Above an App in Portrait Mode</a>&quot; first appeared on <a href="https://www.macrumors.com">MacRumors.com</a><br/><br/><a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/iphone-duo-watch-video-above-an-app-in-portrait-mode.2492836/">Discuss this article</a> in our forums<br/><br/>